# Integrate OpenStreetMap

This plan outlines the steps to add an interactive OpenStreetMap to the app, allowing users to view a map and their current location alongside the AI Pothole Scanner.

## Proposed Changes

We will introduce a bottom navigation bar to switch between the Pothole Scanner and the new Map interface smoothly.

### 1. Add Dependencies
We need to add three essential packages to `pubspec.yaml`:
- **`flutter_map`**: The core package for rendering OpenStreetMap tiles.
- **`latlong2`**: Required for handling Latitude/Longitude map coordinates.
- **`geolocator`**: To request GPS permissions and locate the user on the map.

### 2. Architecture Updates (lib/main.dart)
Modify `main.dart` to support multiple screens natively without interrupting the camera:
- Wrap the main scaffold body in an `IndexedStack` based on a `_currentIndex` variable. The `IndexedStack` ensures the camera doesn't completely rebuild/destroy when we look at the map.
- **Tab 0**: The existing Pothole Scanner UI.
- **Tab 1**: A new `MapScreen` widget.
- Add a `BottomNavigationBar` with icons for "Scanner" and "Map".

### 3. Implement MapScreen Widget
Create the `MapScreen` logic:
- Render a `FlutterMap` widget using the generic OpenStreetMap public tile server (`https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png`).
- Add logic using `geolocator` to request user location and automatically pan the map to the user's current GPS position.

### 4. Native Permissions (Android)
Update `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` to include location access permissions so that `geolocator` can function correctly.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> The `geolocator` plugin requires native Location Permissions on Android. The app will prompt you for GPS access the first time you open the Map tab. I will inject these permissions into your Android configuration automatically.

> [!NOTE]  
> Do you want any specific map features right away, such as plotting a marker on the map whenever the AI detects a pothole, or just a basic map viewer for now?
